    {
      "tool": "lab_docs_read",
      "isError": false,
      "result": {
        "doc_id": "scripts",
        "total_lines": 22,
        "start_line": 1,
        "text": "# Script and configuration API\n\nreward.py defines reward(observation, action, next_observation). For the current synthetic probe, inputs are float32 tensors [batch,61], [batch,14], [batch,61]. Return a finite float32 tensor [batch] on the same device. Slots have NO robot-state meaning in this probe; the template's index 0 is a synthetic feature, not forward velocity.\n\nstrategy.py defines build_policy(observation_dim, action_dim) returning a torch.nn.Module with trainable parameters. The probe moves it to the requested device. It must output finite [batch,14] actions in training and inference mode. This is policy-network authoring; arbitrary PPO algorithm plugins are not implemented.\n\ntraining.json is a strict object with exactly these keys:\n- schema_version: 1\n- task: \"microduck-flat-walk\" (planned task, no environment runner yet)\n- algorithm: \"ppo\" (planned algorithm; the probe is not PPO)\n- training_device: \"cpu\" | \"mps\" | \"cuda\"\n- inference_device: \"cpu\" | \"mps\" | \"cuda\"\n- physics_backend: \"mujoco_cpu\" | \"mujoco_warp_cuda\" (planned environment adapters)\n- seed: integer 0..2147483647\n- max_iterations: integer 1..100000 (reserved for the real runner, not consumed by probe)\n\nlab_backend_probe uses its explicit device argument and the config seed. It performs exactly 3 synthetic optimizer steps, regardless of training_device, inference_device or max_iterations. This permits probing multiple devices against the same immutable revision without pretending the configured training job ran.\n\nDraft writes can contain invalid code/config; validate before executing. Syntax validation does not import code and does not prove safety or numerical correctness. Runtime probe catches invalid output shapes, NaNs, absent gradients and unavailable devices.\n\nFuture real-environment reward API must expose named physical state, units and termination conditions. A deployable artifact must also capture observation order/normalization, action mapping/scales/clips, actuator model, simulation/control timesteps, initial state and model hash. A 61-to-14 tensor shape alone does not establish compatibility. ONNX is an inference artifact, not a resumable PPO checkpoint.\n"
      }
    },
